n an expected boundary. Passing notePath like '../../../../../../etc/passwd' would resolve outside the vault.\",\n      \"category\": \"path-traversal-potential\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"riskScore\": 18,\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    \"Add try-catch blocks around fs.mkdirSync() and fs.writeFileSync() with proper error logging\",\n    \"Implement path boundary validation in external_id.js: verify resolved path is within repoRoot\",\n    \"Add explicit file permissions (0o644 for files, 0o755 for dirs) to fs calls: fs.mkdirSync(dirPath, { mode: 0o755, recursive: true })\",\n    \"Validate/escape YAML frontmatter generation, especially title field, to prevent malformed YAML\",\n    \"Review .env.example comments: ensure production .env files are never committed and use secure secret management (Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, etc.)\",\n    \"Consider using a logging library instead of console.error() for production use\",\n    \"No hardcoded secrets detected ✓ — review actual .env and config files in your deployment for secrets\",\n    \"These are local utility scripts; ensure they're not exposed to untrusted input in any web-facing context\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Summary:** This is a personal knowledge management system (Obsidian vault) using local Node.js bootstrap scripts. **No critical security vulnerabilities found.** Risk is inherently low since these are local tooling scripts without network exposure or database operations. Main improvements needed: error handling, input validation, and explicit file permissions. The codebase follows reasonable practices for its intended use case.\n",
